TinyCBOR fuzzers
----------------

These are libFuzzer-style fuzzers for TinyCBOR, also used by OSS-Fuzz.

  parser_fuzzer     parses the input as a sequence of CBOR items, visiting
                    every item and extracting every value; optionally uses
                    the reader API (cbor_parser_init_reader)
  validate_fuzzer   cbor_value_validate() with any combination of flags
  tojson_fuzzer     cbor_value_to_json_advance() with any combination of flags
  pretty_fuzzer     cbor_value_to_pretty_advance_flags() and
                    cbor_value_to_pretty_stream() with any combination of flags
  encoder_fuzzer    interprets the input as a sequence of encoder commands,
                    then parses the result back and compares it

For all fuzzers except encoder_fuzzer, the first 4 bytes of the input are a
configuration word (flags, mode) and the rest is the CBOR payload. The seed
corpus in corpus/ uses a zero configuration word followed by the CBOR data
from the unit tests; cbor.dict is a dictionary for those fuzzers.

The assert()s in TinyCBOR check that the API is used correctly, so the
fuzzers must be built without NDEBUG: an assertion failure is a bug in the
fuzzer. The fuzzers also abort if the library contradicts its documented
behaviour (for example, if cbor_value_validate() succeeds but parsing the same
data fails).

To build with Clang and libFuzzer:

  cmake -S. -Bbuild -DBUILD_FUZZERS=ON \
        -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++ \
        -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS="-g -O1 -fsanitize=fuzzer-no-link,address,undefined" \
        -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined"
  cmake --build build

LIB_FUZZING_ENGINE selects what to link the fuzzers with (default:
-fsanitize=fuzzer; if set in the environment, as in OSS-Fuzz, that is used).

To run:

  build/fuzz/parser_fuzzer -dict=fuzz/cbor.dict new-corpus fuzz/corpus
